<p>In the latest turn in the Middle East war, President Trump said the United States is negotiating with Iran and has sent a 15-point proposal aimed at ending nearly four weeks of fighting. Multiple reports said the plan reached Tehran through Pakistan and includes at least a temporary ceasefire. Iran’s public response was sharply skeptical: parliamentary speaker Mohammad Bagher Qalibaf denied any talks, and an Iranian military spokesperson said Washington was “negotiating with itself”. Even so, one encouraging sign emerged when Iran said “non-hostile” oil vessels could pass through the Strait of Hormuz, helping push oil prices lower and lift Asian stocks on hopes of de-escalation. At the same time, the conflict kept widening on the ground. Iran launched fresh missile and drone attacks across the region, including toward Israel and US-linked targets in Gulf states, while Israel struck Tehran and other Iranian sites, according to regional and international coverage. In parallel, US media outlets and officials cited by news organizations said Washington is preparing to send roughly 1,000 to 3,000 troops from the 82nd Airborne Division to the Middle East, giving the administration more military options even as it pursues diplomacy. The result is a fast-moving mix of escalation and diplomacy, with markets responding quickly to any sign that a wider regional shutdown might still be avoided.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/E-4bHQMUh0GHuNAznnFbZOFlTstKZlXf_A8LSY0TXmqZAotQCzuIKoxwUfRjcoZukWq843eQZxQMVLMeDnJA56i-yMMN_M3VNXIMnF4tI0p-' alt='US President Donald Trump speaks at the White House in Washington on March 24, 2026, as reports emerged of a US peace proposal to Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Trump’s &quot;gift&quot; comment: Trump said Iran had given the US a &quot;very big present&quot; tied to oil and gas, a remark several reports linked to Tehran’s signal that &quot;non-hostile&quot; vessels could transit the Strait of Hormuz.</li><li>Israeli buy-in remains unclear: Reports on the 15-point US proposal said it was still unclear whether Israel backed the plan, a major variable for any ceasefire effort.</li></ul><blockquote>We&#x27;re in negotiations right now - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: President Trump said senior US officials including Steve Witkoff, Marco Rubio, JD Vance and Jared Kushner were working the Iran file and that Washington was talking to “the right people” in Tehran. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-kushner-witkoff-rubio-and-vance-are-in-negotiations-with-iran-trump-says'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iranian political leadership: Parliament speaker Mohammad Bagher Qalibaf publicly denied that Iran was negotiating with the United States to end the war. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-kushner-witkoff-rubio-and-vance-are-in-negotiations-with-iran-trump-says'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iranian military: A spokesperson for Khatam Al-Anbiya Central Headquarters mocked the US outreach effort and, according to state media, said the United States was negotiating with itself. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-military-spokesperson-says-us-negotiating-itself-state-media'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Gulf states: Kuwait and Saudi Arabia said they had repelled fresh drone attacks as the regional conflict spread. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-strikes-tehran-as-trump-says-us-negotiating-to-end-war'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-kushner-witkoff-rubio-and-vance-are-in-negotiations-with-iran-trump-says'>WATCH: Kushner, Witkoff, Rubio and Vance are &#x27;in negotiations&#x27; with Iran, Trump says</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347813/iranian-military-mocks-trumps-claim-talks-deal'>Iranian military scoffs at US attempts at a ceasefir